<title>UK: Glynwed sells Wednesbury to Mueller.</title>
<headline>Glynwed sells Wednesbury to Mueller.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British industrial holding company Glynwed International Plc said on Monday it would sell Wednesbury Tube to U.S. group Mueller Industries Inc.</p>
<p>Glynwed said the sale price for Wednesbury Tube, a British maker of copper tube, was expected to be fixed at 12.5 million stg. After adjustments for book value and assets, the sale would result in a net loss on the disposal of around 12 million stg.  </p>
<p>Glynwed said Wednesbury employed 440 people. It said the disposal would remove it from copper tube manufacturing.</p>
<p>In 1996 the business generated an operating loss of 300,000 stg on turnover of 58.6 million.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
